    "title": "Pinson Shooting on Highway 75 Leaves One Dead, Three Injured; Suspect in Custody - NewsBreak",
    "text": "11 hours ago On Sunday morning, October 19, 2025, deputies responded to a shooting on the 7900 block of Highway 75 North in Pinson, Alabama. Three people—a 21-year-old man, an 18-year-old man, and an 18-year-old woman—had gunshot wounds and were taken to local hospitals. A fourth victim, a 20-year-old woman, was also hospitalized after arriving by private vehicle. Authorities said the shooting followed an altercation.\nSteven Tyler Whitehead, 27, was arrested and charged with three counts of attempted murder. Each charge carried a $60,000 bond. On October 22, 2025, after one victim died, Whitehead was also charged with murder. This charge has no bond. He is being held at the Jefferson County Jail. The investigation is ongoing. Authorities ask anyone with information to contact the Jefferson County Sheriff’s Office or Crime Stoppers.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
